"""
One viewing of a media title. Its options and capability declaration are fixed when it starts. To change
the playback choice, including picking Original again after it changed to Auto, the client destroys this
playback session and creates a new one with the new choice. The new playback session starts from the top,
with the full format-attempt budget and no format-failure history (ADR 0052).
"""
type PlaybackSession {
    id: ID!
    """
    The format attempts that count against maximumFormatAttempts. The HLS format attempt that an audio switch
    starts from direct play counts none (ADR 0043), and neither does a format attempt that continues an encode in
    software after a hardware encoder failure (ADR 0044), so this can be less than the number of decisions.
    """
    formatAttemptCount: Int!
    "The playback session's format-attempt budget. The default is 4."
    maximumFormatAttempts: Int!
    "The playback choice that the client asked for. A missing quality reads as AUTO."
    requestedChoice: VideoQuality!
    """
    The playback choice that plays now. It equals requestedChoice, except that ORIGINAL changes to AUTO
    once the playback session plays or prepares an encode (ADR 0052). It never changes back within a
    playback session.
    """
    playbackChoice: VideoQuality!
    """
    The latest change from the output that requestedChoice asked for to another output. While it is set, the
    client shows a caution on its quality control and explains the change in its quality picker. Null while
    the playback session plays the output that requestedChoice asked for. Once set, it stays set until the
    playback session ends. A later change can replace it. To play another playback choice, the client starts
    a new playback session, and that playback session's formatChange starts null. When requestedChoice is
    AUTO, only HDR_NOT_KEPT sets it: Auto's other recoveries do not change what the viewer sees, so they are
    not announced. The fallback from direct play to the HLS copy never sets it.
    """
    formatChange: PlaybackFormatChange
    """
    The playback choices that this media title offers, in the order that a quality control lists them:
    ORIGINAL, AUTO, then each fixed quality up to the source's picture size, largest first. A fixed quality
    larger than the source is left out, because its encode would not enlarge the picture.
    """
    offeredChoices: [VideoQuality!]!
    currentFormatAttempt: PlaybackFormatAttempt!
    """
    How each format attempt that started delivers the media title, the initial format first. A format attempt
    that the server refused, or that failed before its stream session started, has no decision. A playback-data
    overlay shows the last decision, and the earlier ones show what a fallback changed.
    """
    decisions: [PlaybackDecision!]!
}

"How one format attempt delivers the media title, and why its output differs from the source."
type PlaybackDecision {
    "The format attempt's number within its playback session: 1 for the initial format."
    formatAttempt: Int!
    "The stream session that the format attempt started."
    streamSessionId: ID!
    video: VideoDelivery!
    "Null when the source has no audio."
    audio: AudioDelivery
    """
    Why the output differs from the source: first the failure of the format attempt before this one, then why
    the source file does not play directly, then the video reasons, then the audio reasons. Each reason appears
    once. Empty when the format attempt plays the source file directly, or copies every track as the source
    holds it in a format attempt that may not direct-play. A copy can carry reasons too, such as an audio encode
    beside a video copy, or Dolby Vision that the copy leaves out.
    """
    reasons: [DecisionReason!]!
    """
    What each video capability entry of the source's codec family refused, so a client can show why the server
    encoded the video or left part of it out. A capability entry accepts an output only when it accepts all of
    it. When direct play was refused, the entries' direct-play refusals come first, then every entry for HLS
    with what it refused of the best copy that this format attempt could plan. Empty for direct play, and for
    HLS when no video capability entry for HLS names the source's codec family, which reasons then name as
    VIDEO_CODEC_NOT_DECLARED.
    """
    videoCapabilityEntryRefusals: [VideoCapabilityEntryRefusal!]!
}

"What one video capability entry refused of a delivery that a format attempt checked."
type VideoCapabilityEntryRefusal {
    delivery: CapabilityEntryDelivery!
    "The entry's position, from 0, among the video capability entries that the client declared."
    entryPosition: Int!
    """
    Each check that the entry refused, in the order the entry checks them. Empty when the entry accepted the
    delivery, so another rule, such as a property issue, ruled it out.
    """
    reasons: [DecisionReason!]!
}

"The delivery for which the server checked a capability entry."
enum CapabilityEntryDelivery {
    "Direct play of the source file from its source container."
    DIRECT_PLAY
    "A stream copy over HLS."
    HLS
}

"How a format attempt delivers one track."
enum PlaybackDelivery {
    "The source file as it is, without HLS."
    DIRECT_PLAY
    "A stream copy of the source's track."
    COPY
    "An encode of the source's track."
    ENCODE
}

type VideoDelivery {
    delivery: PlaybackDelivery!
    source: VideoFormat!
    "The output of the format attempt. For an encode, the largest variant that it offers."
    output: VideoFormat!
}

"The format of a video track. A bitrate is in bits per second."
type VideoFormat {
    "The codec family, such as h264, hevc or av1, or unknown for a source whose probe named no codec."
    codec: String!
    "The displayed picture's width."
    width: Int!
    "The displayed picture's height."
    height: Int!
    "Frames per second. Null when the probe found no frame rate."
    frameRate: Float
    "Null when the probe found no bitrate for the video track."
    bitrate: Int
    videoRange: VideoRange!
    "Whether the track carries Dolby Vision."
    dolbyVision: Boolean!
    "Probe facts for the source, or planned output facts after rewrites and encoding. Null when unavailable."
    details: VideoFormatDetails
}

"These describe the stream, not the HDR mode the player's display actually uses."
type VideoFormatDetails {
    codecProfile: VideoCodecProfile
    "Major times ten plus minor. Null when not known; an encode does not reuse the source's level."
    codecLevel: Int
    bitDepth: Int
    chromaSubsampling: ChromaSubsampling
    compatibleBase: CompatibleBase!
    hdr10Plus: MetadataPresence!
    dolbyVision: DolbyVisionDetails!
    masteringDisplay: VideoMasteringDisplay
    contentLightLevel: VideoContentLightLevel
    "Changes to a copied bitstream. Empty for the source, direct play and encodes."
    bitstreamRewrites: [BitstreamRewrite!]!
}

enum ChromaSubsampling { CHROMA_420 CHROMA_422 CHROMA_444 MONOCHROME }

"PQ is the SMPTE ST 2084 Perceptual Quantizer transfer function; it alone does not prove HDR10."
enum CompatibleBase { UNSPECIFIED SDR PQ HLG NONE }

enum MetadataPresence { UNSPECIFIED ABSENT PRESENT }

type DolbyVisionDetails {
    presence: MetadataPresence!
    "Profile from the configuration record. Null when the record does not name one."
    profile: Int
    level: Int
    "For example, profile 8 with compatibility identifier 1 is profile 8.1."
    baseLayerCompatibilityId: Int
    enhancementLayer: DolbyVisionEnhancementLayer
    observedRpu: MetadataPresence
}

enum DolbyVisionEnhancementLayer { UNSPECIFIED NONE MEL FEL }

"Mastering display luminance in cd/m² (nits). Null means no stored or planned metadata."
type VideoMasteringDisplay { minLuminance: Float! maxLuminance: Float! }

"Content light levels in cd/m² (nits). A declared zero means unknown, as CTA-861.3 specifies."
type VideoContentLightLevel { maxContentLightLevel: Int! maxFrameAverageLightLevel: Int! }

enum BitstreamRewrite {
    STRIP_DOLBY_VISION
    STRIP_HDR10_PLUS
    NORMALIZE_DOLBY_VISION_RECORD
    "Removes the enhancement layer and rewrites RPUs without the FEL residual."
    CONVERT_DOLBY_VISION_PROFILE_7_TO_8_1
}

type AudioDelivery {
    delivery: PlaybackDelivery!
    source: AudioFormat!
    output: AudioFormat!
}

"The format of an audio track. A bitrate is in bits per second."
type AudioFormat {
    "The codec, such as aac, ac3, eac3, flac or opus."
    codec: String!
    "Null when the probe found no channel count for the source's audio track."
    channels: Int
    "Null when the probe found no bitrate for the audio track."
    bitrate: Int
}

"""
Why a format attempt's output differs from its source: why the source file does not play directly, why the
server encodes the video or the audio, or what a copy leaves out. The stream decision names each reason as it
decides, so the reasons agree with the output. When no entry accepts a copy, "the closest entry" is the client's video
capability entry for HLS of the source's codec family that refuses the fewest properties. When an entry accepts a copy
only after the copy leaves out Dolby Vision or HDR10+, "the closest entry" is that accepting entry, and the reasons name
what it refused in the copies that kept more.
"""
enum DecisionReason {
    "No video capability entry for HLS names the source's codec family."
    VIDEO_CODEC_NOT_DECLARED
    "The closest entry does not list the source's codec profile."
    VIDEO_CODEC_PROFILE_NOT_DECLARED
    "The source's codec level or tier is above the closest entry's maximum for its profile."
    VIDEO_CODEC_LEVEL_NOT_DECLARED
    "The source's bit depth is above the closest entry's maximum."
    VIDEO_BIT_DEPTH_NOT_DECLARED
    "The probe reported no bit depth for the source's video, so no entry can accept a copy."
    VIDEO_BIT_DEPTH_UNKNOWN
    "The source's picture is larger than the closest entry's maximum."
    VIDEO_PICTURE_SIZE_NOT_DECLARED
    "The source's frame rate is above the closest entry's maximum."
    VIDEO_FRAME_RATE_NOT_DECLARED
    "The closest entry does not declare the source's compatible base: SDR, PQ or HLG."
    DYNAMIC_RANGE_NOT_DECLARED
    "The viewer chose SDR in a fixed quality, and a copy would keep the source's HDR range, so the server encodes SDR."
    VIEWER_CHOSE_SDR
    "The closest entry does not declare the source's Dolby Vision profile and level."
    DOLBY_VISION_NOT_DECLARED
    "The probe found no Dolby Vision profile or level for the source, so no entry can accept its Dolby Vision."
    DOLBY_VISION_PROFILE_OR_LEVEL_UNKNOWN
    "The closest entry does not declare HDR10+."
    HDR10_PLUS_NOT_DECLARED
    "A copy that keeps Dolby Vision strips the source's HDR10+ information, whatever the client declares."
    HDR10_PLUS_STRIPPED_BESIDE_DOLBY_VISION
    "The source's picture is larger than the fixed quality or the maximum size that the client sent."
    PICTURE_ABOVE_VIEWER_LIMIT
    "A copy costs more than the client's maximum bitrate beside every audio step."
    BITRATE_ABOVE_VIEWER_LIMIT
    "The source is interlaced. HLS delivery needs progressive video, and direct play of an interlaced file is unmeasured."
    SOURCE_INTERLACED
    "The source's HDR base was probed before the probe described its codec profile."
    VIDEO_PROPERTIES_NOT_PROBED
    "The source's Dolby Vision configuration claims another base than the source's transfer signals."
    DOLBY_VISION_COMPATIBILITY_DISAGREES_WITH_TRANSFER
    "The source's Dolby Vision RPUs start their samples, so a copy or direct play would hand players misplaced RPUs."
    DOLBY_VISION_RPU_STARTS_SAMPLE
    "The source is H.264 at another bit depth or chroma subsampling than 8-bit 4:2:0."
    H264_NOT_8_BIT_4_2_0
    "The probe reported no chroma subsampling for the source's H.264 video."
    VIDEO_CHROMA_SUBSAMPLING_UNKNOWN
    "The source's sample entry is not one under which a playlist describes a copy, such as hev1."
    SAMPLE_ENTRY_NOT_COPYABLE
    "The probe stored no codec string for the source's video, which a playlist needs to describe a copy."
    VIDEO_CODEC_STRING_UNKNOWN
    "The probe could not name the source's codec profile."
    VIDEO_CODEC_PROFILE_UNKNOWN
    "The probe reported no codec name for the source's video."
    VIDEO_CODEC_UNKNOWN
    "The probe stored no video facts for a copy."
    VIDEO_SOURCE_NOT_COPYABLE
    "The source's keyframe positions are not known yet."
    KEYFRAMES_UNKNOWN
    "No source keyframe lies between the start and the end of the media, so no copied segment opens."
    KEYFRAMES_TOO_SPARSE
    "The source's keyframe timestamps go backwards or out of range."
    KEYFRAME_TIMESTAMPS_INVALID
    "The probe stored no start time correction for the source's container, which a copy needs to start its segments at the source's keyframes."
    START_TIME_CORRECTION_UNKNOWN
    "A copied segment, with the audio beside it, would be larger than a segment may be."
    SEGMENT_EXCEEDS_CAP
    "No connected worker can make the copy's planned output."
    NO_WORKER_DELIVERS_COPY
    "No audio capability entry for HLS names the source's audio codec."
    AUDIO_CODEC_NOT_DECLARED
    "The source has more audio channels than the entry for its codec accepts."
    AUDIO_CHANNELS_NOT_DECLARED
    """
    The probe reported no channel count for the source's audio, and the entry for its codec accepts fewer channels than
    the stereo track the server then assumes.
    """
    AUDIO_CHANNELS_UNKNOWN
    "HLS delivery cannot copy the source's audio codec profile, such as AAC Main."
    AUDIO_SOURCE_NOT_COPYABLE
    "The probe stored no codec string for the source's audio, which a playlist needs to describe a copy."
    AUDIO_CODEC_STRING_UNKNOWN
    """
    The source's FLAC minimum block size is below the minimum of each audio entry for HLS that accepts the rest of the
    copy.
    """
    AUDIO_BLOCK_SIZE_NOT_DECLARED
    """
    The probe stored no FLAC minimum block size for the source's audio, and each audio entry for HLS that accepts the
    rest of the copy gives a minimum.
    """
    AUDIO_BLOCK_SIZE_UNKNOWN
    """
    The client's maximum bitrate takes a lower audio step. The output can still exceed a maximum below the lowest
    audio and video rates that the server encodes.
    """
    AUDIO_LOWERED_FOR_BITRATE_LIMIT
    "The source's video ends at least one segment before another stream of the source, so the encode holds its last frame to the end."
    VIDEO_ENDS_EARLY
    "The audio ends at least one segment before another stream of the source, so the encode pads it with silence to the end."
    AUDIO_ENDS_EARLY
    "The probe found no single source container that a client can declare for direct play."
    SOURCE_CONTAINER_UNKNOWN
    """
    No video capability entry of the source's codec family lists the file's source container for direct play, or,
    for a file with audio, no audio capability entry lists it.
    """
    DIRECT_PLAY_CONTAINER_NOT_DECLARED
    """
    No video capability entry that lists the MP4 or MOV container lists the video stream's sample entry, such as
    hev1, or the probe stored no sample entry.
    """
    DIRECT_PLAY_SAMPLE_ENTRY_NOT_DECLARED
    """
    No video capability entry that lists the file's source container accepts every property of the video stream as
    it is, or the probe left one of those properties unknown.
    """
    DIRECT_PLAY_VIDEO_NOT_DECLARED
    "An audio track of the file is one that no audio capability entry listing the file's source container accepts."
    DIRECT_PLAY_AUDIO_NOT_DECLARED
    """
    The player cannot select an audio track inside a file that it direct-plays, and it would not start on the audio
    track that the viewer chose: the viewer chose a later track, or the file marks another track as its default. The
    format attempt that the viewer's audio switch moves from direct play to HLS names it too.
    """
    DIRECT_PLAY_AUDIO_TRACK_NOT_SELECTABLE
    "A forced image subtitle track, PGS, VobSub or DVB, is in the language of an audio track."
    FORCED_IMAGE_SUBTITLE_IN_AUDIO_LANGUAGE
    "The direct play of the format attempt before this one failed, so this one plays over HLS."
    DIRECT_PLAY_FAILED
    "The copy of the format attempt before this one failed, so this one encodes the video."
    COPY_FAILED
    "The encode of the format attempt before this one failed, so this one encodes in another codec family."
    ENCODE_FAILED
    """
    The Dolby Vision copy of the format attempt before this one failed, so this one copies the video with its Dolby
    Vision stripped, or encodes it when the client or the workers rule that copy out.
    """
    DOLBY_VISION_COPY_FAILED
    """
    The hardware encoder of the format attempt before this one failed, so this one encodes the same codec family with
    the software encoder. That format attempt does not count against maximumFormatAttempts (ADR 0044).
    """
    HARDWARE_ENCODER_FAILED
}

"Why the output differs from the output that the requested playback choice asked for (ADR 0052)."
enum PlaybackFormatChange {
    "An HLS copy failed: the player refused it, the worker could not make it, or it ran short while a source stream still had media. An encode plays."
    COPY_FAILED
    "Direct play failed and the server rules out the HLS copy. An encode plays."
    DIRECT_PLAY_FAILED
    "Original could neither direct-play nor copy the source, so its first format attempt is an encode."
    STARTED_WITH_ENCODE
    "A Dolby Vision copy failed, so the same copy without Dolby Vision plays on the source's PQ or HLG base."
    DOLBY_VISION_STRIPPED
    "The viewer switched audio tracks during direct play and the server rules out the HLS copy. An encode plays."
    AUDIO_TRACK_SWITCHED
    """
    The source's HDR range was not kept, and SDR plays. The server sets it when a format attempt plays SDR of
    a PQ or HLG source in one of two cases: the client sent dynamicRange HDR with a fixed quality, or an
    earlier format attempt of the playback session played PQ or HLG. The server sets it only while no other
    value is set, so a failed copy whose encode plays SDR stays COPY_FAILED. It clears as every value does:
    when the playback session ends.
    """
    HDR_NOT_KEPT
}

union PlaybackFormatAttempt = PendingPlaybackFormatAttempt | ReadyPlaybackFormatAttempt | FailedPlaybackFormatAttempt

type PendingPlaybackFormatAttempt {
    streamSessionId: ID!
}

type ReadyPlaybackFormatAttempt {
    streamSession: StreamSession!
}

type FailedPlaybackFormatAttempt {
    streamSessionId: ID!
    error: PlaybackFormatAttemptError!
}

union PlaybackFormatAttemptError = StartPositionOutOfRangeError | PlaybackOutputMismatchError | PlaybackInvalidSpecificationError | PlaybackFormatRejectedError | PlaybackFormatAttemptsExhaustedError | PlaybackStartupFailedError | MediaFileNotFoundError | MediaFileProbeNotReadyError | InvalidMediaFileError | MediaFileHasNoVideoError | MediaFileFrameRateUnknownError | TranscodeCapacityUnavailableError | NoEligibleVideoFormatError

enum PlaybackFormatFailure {
    UNSUPPORTED_FORMAT
    DECODE_ERROR
}

input CreatePlaybackSessionInput {
    mediaFileId: ID!
    options: StreamingOptionsInput
    "What the client's current player and display accept."
    capabilities: ClientCapabilityDeclarationInput!
    """
    Where playback starts, in seconds from the start of the media, such as the viewer's resume position.
    It must be 0 or more and less than the media's duration. The server refuses any other value with
    StartPositionOutOfRangeError. An HLS stream session starts its first job attempt at the segment that
    holds this position, and its multivariant playlist marks the position with EXT-X-START. A direct-play
    stream session returns the position, and the client seeks the file there. A later format attempt
    starts at this position too, until the client reports a playback position in another second. Null
    starts playback at the beginning of the media.
    """
    startPositionSeconds: Float
}

type CreatePlaybackSessionPayload {
    playbackSession: PlaybackSession
    userErrors: [CreatePlaybackSessionError!]!
}

union CreatePlaybackSessionError = InvalidIdError | PlaybackSessionClosedError | StartPositionOutOfRangeError | MediaFileNotFoundError | MediaFileProbeNotReadyError | InvalidMediaFileError | MediaFileHasNoVideoError | MediaFileFrameRateUnknownError | TranscodeCapacityUnavailableError | NoEligibleVideoFormatError | CapabilityValuesRequiredError | HlsAacCapabilityRequiredError | CapabilityListTooLongError | CapabilityMaximumInvalidError | CapabilityProfileMismatchError | VideoCodecTierInvalidError | AudioMinBlockSizeInvalidError

input ReportPlaybackFormatFailureInput {
    playbackSessionId: ID!
    streamSessionId: ID!
    "A player error about the media format itself. Network, server, file and authorization errors are not format failures."
    reason: PlaybackFormatFailure!
}

type ReportPlaybackFormatFailurePayload {
    playbackSession: PlaybackSession
    userErrors: [ReportPlaybackFormatFailureError!]!
}

union ReportPlaybackFormatFailureError = InvalidIdError | PlaybackSessionClosedError

input SwitchPlaybackAudioTrackInput {
    playbackSessionId: ID!
    "The direct-play stream session that plays now."
    streamSessionId: ID!
    """
    The audio track that the viewer chose: its position, counting from 0, among the file's audio tracks in
    stream order, as DirectPlayStreamSession.audioTrackPosition counts.
    """
    audioTrackPosition: Int!
}

type SwitchPlaybackAudioTrackPayload {
    playbackSession: PlaybackSession
    userErrors: [SwitchPlaybackAudioTrackError!]!
}

union SwitchPlaybackAudioTrackError = InvalidIdError | PlaybackSessionClosedError | AudioTrackNotInFileError | PlaybackStartupFailedError | StartPositionOutOfRangeError | MediaFileNotFoundError | MediaFileProbeNotReadyError | InvalidMediaFileError | MediaFileHasNoVideoError | MediaFileFrameRateUnknownError | TranscodeCapacityUnavailableError | NoEligibleVideoFormatError

"The file has no audio track at the position that the input names."
type AudioTrackNotInFileError implements InputMutationError & MutationError {
    message: String!
    inputPath: [String!]!
}

input DestroyPlaybackSessionInput {
    playbackSessionId: ID!
}

type DestroyPlaybackSessionPayload {
    playbackSessionId: ID
    userErrors: [DestroyPlaybackSessionError!]!
}

union DestroyPlaybackSessionError = InvalidIdError

type PlaybackSessionClosedError implements MutationError {
    message: String!
}

type PlaybackOutputMismatchError implements MutationError {
    message: String!
}

type PlaybackInvalidSpecificationError implements MutationError {
    message: String!
}

type PlaybackFormatRejectedError implements MutationError {
    message: String!
    reason: PlaybackFormatFailure!
}

type PlaybackFormatAttemptsExhaustedError implements MutationError {
    message: String!
}

type PlaybackStartupFailedError implements MutationError {
    message: String!
}

"The start position lies before 0, or at or past the end of the media."
type StartPositionOutOfRangeError implements InputMutationError & MutationError {
    message: String!
    inputPath: [String!]!
}
